Theorem CN-1: Dead-Absent bidirectional implication

  Preconditions:
    - s is an AimsState with all dimensions instantiated
      per the canonical proof notation sec-Per-Dimension-Symbol-Set
      (working-hypothesis 7-dim: Access, Consumption, Cardinality,
       Uniqueness, Locality, Shape, Effect)
    - s = (O, Dead, 1, u, bl, Phi, {})
      i.e. Access=O, Consumption=Dead, Cardinality=1, Uniqueness=u,
           Locality=bl, Shape=Phi, Effect={}
    - canonicalize(s) is s with CN-1 + CN-2 applied per
      Annex E §AIMS (bounded loop, max 3 rounds to fixpoint)

  Soundness property:
    Forall s in AimsState.
      s.consumption = Dead implies canonicalize(s).cardinality = Absent
    Forall s in AimsState.
      s.cardinality = Absent implies canonicalize(s).consumption = Dead

  Proof obligation:
    Case analysis on (s.consumption, s.cardinality):
      Case (Dead, Absent):
        Premise vacuously satisfied on both directions;
        canonicalize(s) = s (idempotent per L-7);
        s.cardinality = Absent and s.consumption = Dead;
        both implications hold.
      Case (Dead, 1):
        CN-1 fires: Cardinality := Absent;
        result state has consumption=Dead, cardinality=Absent;
        forward direction (Dead implies Absent) discharged;
        reverse direction premise (Absent) false in input state, vacuous.
      Case (Dead, omega):
        CN-1 fires: Cardinality := Absent;
        same as Case (Dead, 1).
      Case (Linear, Absent):
        CN-1 fires: Consumption := Dead;
        result state has consumption=Dead, cardinality=Absent;
        reverse direction (Absent implies Dead) discharged;
        forward direction premise (Dead) false in input state, vacuous.
      Case (Affine, Absent):
        CN-1 fires: Consumption := Dead;
        same as Case (Linear, Absent).
      Case (Unrestricted, Absent):
        CN-1 fires: Consumption := Dead;
        same as Case (Linear, Absent).
      All remaining cases (consumption in {Linear, Affine, Unrestricted}
       and cardinality in {1, omega}):
        Both premises false; vacuously satisfied.

    Lattice validation:
      CN-1 mutates only Consumption + Cardinality dimensions
      per Annex E §AIMS CN-1; Access=O, Locality=bl, Shape=Phi,
      Effect={} preserved across canonicalization.

    Monotonicity (L-6) on Consumption x Cardinality sub-lattice:
      Sub-lattice carrier:
        Consumption: Dead < Linear < Affine < Unrestricted (height 3)
        Cardinality: Absent < 1 < omega (height 2)
      Each canonicalization step is monotone: applying CN-1 to a state
      where s.consumption = Dead and s.cardinality > Absent moves the
      state DOWN the Cardinality dimension (omega -> Absent or 1 -> Absent);
      this preserves the partial order under the dual lattice ordering
      consistent with L-6's monotone-transfer requirement on the
      canonicalization map.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (for the Dead/Absent enumeration above)
      lattice (validates Access/Locality/Shape/Effect preservation)
      monotonicity (L-6 on Consumption x Cardinality sub-lattice)

  Expected:
    status: unimplemented_engine_shape
    reason: scaffold-time; engine implementations pending
